  "problem": "The owner of a restaurant noted that $145$ vegetarian customers visited his restaurant during a particular week. On a particular day of the same week, he noted that $x=15$ vegetarian customers visited the restaurant, corresponding to a $z$-score of $z=-1.5.$ Find the standard deviation of the number of vegetarian customers per day, giving your answer to $2$ decimal places.",
